2026-08-16T08:21:57.2656261Z [36;1m# Compile on every core the runner has, not the two this used to pin.[0m
2026-08-16T08:21:57.2656862Z [36;1m# Standard GitHub-hosted Linux runners have been 4-vCPU since 2024, so[0m
2026-08-16T08:21:57.2657329Z [36;1m# -j2 left half the box idle through the phase that dominates a build:[0m
2026-08-16T08:21:57.2657779Z [36;1m# measured on a 4-core box, 8 vendored unity objects with ccache[0m
2026-08-16T08:21:57.2658221Z [36;1m# disabled take 70.8 s at -j2 and 43.1 s at -j4 -- 1.64x, at identical[0m
2026-08-16T08:21:57.2658669Z [36;1m# user time. Peak RSS per unity object is ~834 MB, so four in flight is[0m
2026-08-16T08:21:57.2659027Z [36;1m# ~3.3 GB of the runner's 16 GB.[0m
2026-08-16T08:21:57.2659381Z [36;1m# detectCores() can return NA on exotic platforms; fall back to the old[0m
