2026-08-16T08:22:09.0324280Z [36;1m## -- Detect an unreleased R --[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0324992Z [36;1m# The persistent ccache below is keyed on getRversion(), and that key is[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0325895Z [36;1m# only honest for a released R, where the version number changes[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0326799Z [36;1m# whenever the installation does. R-devel is rebuilt every day but keeps[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0327727Z [36;1m# reporting the same number for months, so one cache entry ends up[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0328600Z [36;1m# serving an arbitrary span of R-devel snapshots -- and restoring it in[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0329479Z [36;1m# the rcc R-devel job has produced build failures. Skip the persistent[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0330368Z [36;1m# cache there and build cold; ccache itself stays configured by the[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0331147Z [36;1m# install action, so reuse within the job is unaffected.[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0331735Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0332240Z [36;1m# R.version$status is empty for a released R and non-empty for one that[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0333464Z [36;1m# moves under a fixed version number ("Under development (unstable)" for[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0334414Z [36;1m# R-devel, "Patched" for R-patched) -- exactly the builds the key cannot[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0335346Z [36;1m# tell apart.[0m
2026-08-16T08:22:09.0336229Z [36;1mecho "DUCKDB_R_UNRELEASED=$(Rscript --vanilla -e 'cat(if (nzchar(R.version$status)) "1" else "0")')" | tee -a $GITHUB_ENV[0m
